  "term": "speech and language disorder",
  "definition": "A speech and language disorder is a problem affecting spoken communication, including speech production and language understanding or expression. In the supplied source, it is described as involving disrupted speech-motor control and, in some cases, severe receptive and expressive language impairments.",
